prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a 3D exploded view of a smartwatch, with all parts modeled procedurally, and output it as a single HTML file.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Include the following importmap in the page, and use <script type="module"> to import three and addons as ES Modules:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>

[Parts (8 Total; Each Must Be an Independent, Pickable Mesh/Object3D)]
(1) Watch body: a metal enclosure made from CylinderGeometry flattened by setting scale.y to a relatively small value;
(2) Screen: PlaneGeometry, with a glass-like appearance and emissive illumination to simulate being lit;
(3) Crown: a small cylinder;
(4) Back case: a thin cylinder/disc separated from the watch body;
(5) Battery: BoxGeometry;
(6) PCB: thin BoxGeometry with a green material;
(7) Strap top: ExtrudeGeometry (extruded along a path) or a bent approximation made with BoxGeometry;
(8) Strap bottom: same as above;
Materials: use distinct MeshStandardMaterial/MeshPhysicalMaterial materials to differentiate the metal watch body, glass screen, rubber straps, and other parts.

[Exploded View Controls]
- A slider with id="explodeSlider", type="range", min=0 max=1 step=0.01, and a default value of 0;
- When explode=0, all parts are in their assembled positions; when explode=1, each part moves outward along its own "explosion direction" (the world-space direction of a preset local normal/axis for each part);
- When the slider value changes, use requestAnimationFrame to smoothly interpolate each part's position toward its target position (equivalent to a TWEEN easing effect; no additional library is required).

[Interaction]
- Clicking a part must highlight it using emissive, and display the part name and a short description in the DOM panel with id="partInfo" (the text must be non-empty);
- Use OrbitControls (from three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js); a button with id="autoRotateBtn" must toggle controls.autoRotate on/off.

[HUD (Must Be Updated in Sync with __3D_STATE__)]
- id="partCount": the number of parts (must be 8);
- id="selectedPart": the name of the currently selected part (when no part is selected, it may display "—" or be empty);
- id="explodePct": the explosion percentage (an integer or one decimal place from 0–100, consistent with the slider).

[State Exposure (Update Every Frame or Immediately After Interaction)]
window.__3D_STATE__ = {
  partCount: number,
  parts: [{ name: string, x: number, y: number, z: number, selected: boolean }, ...],
  explodeValue: number,
  selectedPart: string | null,
  autoRotate: boolean
}

Output a single HTML file.
